WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:04.400
-Come on! That's a movie star.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.434
That is a movie star!
You're a stud.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.000
Thank you for coming back.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.734
And thank you --
I don't know if you saw.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.501
There was a sketch earlier
that looked --

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.734
a character that looked like
you, Goat-Leg Greg.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:13.801
-Who was that guy?

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:14.968
-I don't know,
but he's a good actor.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.667
I love him.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:19.834
Was there ever a bizarre role
that you ever said yes to?

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.234
You were like --
-Yeah, that one.

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:22.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.200
-I want to start by saying,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.868
you've had an
incredible, incredible year.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.334
It's got to be probably an
incredible few years.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.901
You're waiting for
all this stuff to come out.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.767
-Yeah.
-What does it feel like?

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.300
You're winning all these awards.
You just won the SAG Award.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.734
You're nominated for --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.901
You're nominated for
an Academy Award.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.234
We're all --
We all love you here.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.300
Has it been a whirlwind?
or what does it feel like?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.901
-Yes. It's been humbling,
to tell you the truth.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:52.000
-Really?
-A lot happens all at once.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.501
And I've been really happy
to get to know

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.634
all of the other nominees
in the category.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:02.367
We have a profound respect
for each other

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.601
that we've been through,
like, this gauntlet

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:05.701
in the last -- I don't know --

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.167
six, eight weeks,
whatever it's been.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.834
-I mean, one of your
first breakout roles was

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.167
in "Encino Man."

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.167
Hold your applau--
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.701
Hold your applause.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.300
They clap before
I could make the joke.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.901
But Ke Huy Quan
was in "Encino Man."

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:21.534
I didn't even remember
this scene.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:24.501
And now you're both
nominated for Academy Awards.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.734
Did you get to --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.501
Isn't that cool?
-It was so great.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:28.734
-Isn't that cool?

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:32.000
-We saw each other at
an actors' round table,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.267
where we, you know,
met everybody at first.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.167
And it's like, "Ke, you're here

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:38.667
and I'm here
and we're still...here."

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.734
You know? He was like,
"Yes, we are!

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:43.267
We're still here."
-"We're still here!" Yes!

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.234
You are definitely still here.
How exciting -- How fun is that?

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:49.200
I watched the SAG Awards,
and you had a very nice moment

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.467
where you talked about
what it felt like to get your

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.534
Screen Actors Guild card,
to get your card.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.801
-Yes.
-It's a big deal.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.100
-It's huge.
It's like being made.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.434
You know, you -- It's --
"Willy Wonka" is for beginners.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.434
-Yes. You want to walk around
and just show it

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.701
to everyone like, "I'm in
the Screen Actors Guild!

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.033
I'm an actor!"
-You're in the club, you know?

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.200
-Yes!

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.968
-And it's an infinite world
of possibilities.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.667
Now all you've got to do is just
go out there and find a job.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:13.901
-Yeah. Well,
that's a different thing.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.200
That's a different thing.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.000
But your first role was
one of my favorite movies,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.367
"Dogfight" with River Phoenix.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:24.534
Here you are in --
-That's me as Sailor Number 1.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.934
-Sailor Number 1 was --
Not a bad movie to be in.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.801
-Number-one sailor.
-You're the number-one sailor.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.767
Do you remember your line?
-I do.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:32.968
This was a film with
River Phoenix.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.133
-I love it.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:35.534
He's one of
my all-time favorites, River.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.734
-He was a sweet guy.
-Do you remember your line?

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.300
-I do remember it, yeah.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.534
-Would you perform it
for us tonight?

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.634
-As you wish. I will.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.667
You ready?
-Quest, can I get a drumroll?

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.701
-To, like...
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:47.701
-Wow.
-You ready?

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.400
-Yes.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.300
Which camera here?
-I didn't write it.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.701
-Yeah, here we go.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.367
-How'd you like to
eat my [bleep]

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:56.400
-There you go.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:04.534
-I got my card.
-SAG card. SAG card.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.434
Wow!

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.267
That is so good. Thank you.
-You're welcome for that.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:12.133
-I also saw you reunite
with Adam Sandler.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.834
I think that was one of
my other favorite movies

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.100
that you were in, "Airheads."

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.567
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.667
-And you and "Sandman" --
lookit.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:20.834
Here's you
and Adam Sandler there.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:24.334
-Steve Buscemi.
-Steve -- That's right.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.067
And you got to sit down with
Adam for some round-table thing,

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.100
and he was talking.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.167
And what did he say to you?

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:31.734
-He told me that
he got me the job.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:33.033
-I did not know that.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.367
-Yeah, I didn't know
that either.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:38.467
And I later learned that that's
a bunch of malarkey.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.234
-Here's why we love Sandler.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.267
So, the whole time
he's talking --

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.400
-He punked me.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.234
It's a 25-year joke
he pulled on me.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.434
-I can't believe it.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.133
-And then Michael Lehmann
went and tweeted out,

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.367
"Uh, no, we hired Brendan
before we had --"

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:52.701
-Yeah, he actually --
-Oh, you found it.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.067
-Yeah, I have the tweet
right here.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.067
Sandler didn't say he fought
for Brendan.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.200
"My recollection,
we cast Brendan before Sandler."

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.067
That's correct.
But good on Adam.

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.133
Good on Sandman.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.200
Why not play around
and have fun?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.501
-He got me.
-He got you good.

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:05.934
-He got me.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.834
-Can we -- Let's talk about
"The Whale," okay?

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:10.334
It's directed by
Darren Aronofsky,

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:11.701
brilliant director.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.934
Oh, my gosh.
Brooklyn boy, by the way.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:17.100
And he came on the show
and he said, "It was just --

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.200
I had the script.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.267
We had the idea.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.000
I just couldn't find the role --

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.133
who can play
the role of Charlie."

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.734
And then you --
He saw you in something.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.133
And he goes, "Oh, my gosh.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.634
Brendan Fraser --
that's who should play --"

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:33.834
And did he call you up and go,
"Hey, I wrote this for you,

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.267
you got the gig," or --

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.567
-I didn't know I had the job.
I knew I had a meeting with him.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:38.834
And I was
a little bit intimidated,

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.334
'cause, you know,
he's Darren Aronofsky.

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:42.167
And I really admire his films
a great deal.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:45.734
And he told me it was about
a man who's been living alone,

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:48.033
he's been harming himself
by overeating,

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.634
and he has regrets
because he wants to

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.200
reunite with
his estranged daughter,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.467
and he has
very little time left.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:56.000
And it's a very specific cast --
I mean, role to cast

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.901
because of the -- because of --
as how he presents.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.934
And so it meant that we had to
work with, as he explained,

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.834
a lot of prosthetic makeup
to create the character.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.067
-Who's the mastermind
behind that?

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.501
-Adrien Morot.

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:11.067
-Adrien Morot --
give everything to.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.300
-And then he went on
and he did "M3GAN,"

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.534
just so you know who he is.

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.701
-Wow! Really? Is that right?
-Yeah. That's his.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:19.167
-He -- The effects,
the special effects --

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.567
-Cool, right?

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.934
If it wasn't a seamless,
then you wouldn't have a movie,

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.767
you know,
because we wouldn't believe it.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.534
And you have to,
because that character

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:29.234
is automatically going to be
me, you know,

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:32.067
reintroduced, in a way,
and everyone's probably

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.267
at first gonna see it and go,

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:34.501
"Oh, is that
George of the Jungle?"

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:37.200
You know, like,
and it is in a way.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.267
But after like five minutes,
you get to know the character,

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.934
you just accept who he is,

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.033
and you go on
this journey of redemption.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.400
-How long did that take
for you to get --

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.901
-Four hours to get in and
about an hour to get out of it.

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.701
But we had a great --
Don't pity me, really.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:50.868
-No, I -- No, no.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.667
No, but I've just got to
think about it myself.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.334
You get there
and you get to set.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:55.934
You've got to show up
early, four hours.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:57.067
Then you have to act.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:58.634
-Yeah, but Adrian
got there an hour before

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.901
and he had to leave
an hour afterwards, too.

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:03.334
-Oh, my gosh.
But you crushed it, buddy.

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:06.334
Even just looking at your face,
I can't even tell you --

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:09.400
It was just so, like -- I wanted
to -- It was just heartbreaking.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.267
-It feels like he's a guy
that you know, I think.

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:12.901
That's what I felt like
when I read it.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:15.033
-That's a guy that you know
and you're rooting for him.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.234
-You care for him.

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.701
-You want him
to figure it out and change,

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:19.367
and you go like,
"I'm going through some stuff."

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.000
And you go, "Yeah, it's fixable.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.367
I want to fix this person or
help you in any way possible."

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.868
-The good news is that
the Obesity Action Coalition

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:27.334
is an advocacy group
that we worked with,

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:29.267
and since the film came out,
the number of people

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:32.734
who have reached out to them to
ask for help has gone way up.

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:35.434
-Yes! Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:39.334
I can't even say it
happened to a greater guy.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.667
You're a good man.
Congratulations.

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:41.901
-Thanks, Jimmy.
-Brendan Fraser.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.033
I want to show a clip.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.667
Here's Brendan Fraser in
"The Whale."

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.434
Take a look.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:50.000
-Do you feel lightheaded,
Charlie? Look at me.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.033
-She's trying to help him.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:52.567
-Who?

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:54.534
-Ellie.

00:06:54.534 --> 00:06:57.267
She was trying to help him.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.133
She just wanted to
send him home.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:07.767
Do you ever get the feeling
that people

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:11.834
are incapable of not caring?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.200
People are amazing.

00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:22.767
-Hong Chau.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.734
-Hong Chau. Great.
-Also nominated.

00:07:24.734 --> 00:07:26.834
-Oh, yeah.
Brendan Fraser, everyone.

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:28.968
"The Whale" is in theaters
and on demand now.

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:30.133
Congratulations.

